# Chat Check

When the user asks for a **Chat Check**:

1. Verify the intended changes and project documentation are committed and pushed to `bobbyzhang133-star/Duck-Plan-Test`.
2. Never publish or deploy the website as part of a Chat Check.
3. Ask the user's Duck Plan ChatGPT project to inspect the current GitHub version and compare it with the repository plan and acceptance criteria.
4. Include the current commit identifier and any review focus specified by the user.
5. Ask for concrete mismatches, source-level causes, severity, and recommended next changes; do not ask for vague general feedback.
6. Report where the review request was sent and summarize the response when one is available.

Example: “Chat Check, focus on lettering” means push the test repository, then request a plan-compliance review centered on whether fur-formed words are readable at production button size.
